Description:

The length of a base64-encoded message body is now computed in a width wide
enough to hold it.  Previously that length was computed in a signed 32-bit
integer while the encoder went on to write output sized from the original
body, so a body whose encoded form exceeded the range of that integer was
given a buffer smaller than the data written into it.  Sites that set
:imapdconf:`maxmessagesize` to a value below roughly 1.5GB were not affected;
the option defaults to no limit at all.


